_r3_1} of the replacement's served jobs in its first two ten-round age bins, C$^*$ audits \site{r_hon_cs_0} and \site{r_hon_cs_1} (its lowest bin; \site{r_hon_cs_2} in the next), and B3 about \site{r_hon_b3_0}. Under R3 the replacement earns less per round (relative to C$^*$, a fraction of \site{r_hon_rel}; the registered diagnostic stores bin means, so no interval is available) and loses more receipts to refunds paid to buyers on false audit failures; R3 directs more of the fixed audit capacity to this provider, which does not show higher total audit spending. Both decisions are about the prescribed search procedure: the D2+H3 test uses search-flagged cells, and the X7-SC test uses them through its references (addendum); their nominal error guarantees are not established on the fresh, selected-rule distributions (Section~\ref{sec:design}).
