+\section*{Use of AI tools}\label{sec:ai-use}
+AI tools were used throughout this work; responsibility for all of it rests with the author. AI coding assistants (Anthropic's Claude models) wrote most of the simulator, analysis, test and release code to the author's specifications, and drafted parts of the text; the author set the research questions, the registered hypotheses, decision rules and every amendment, and checked and revised all text. Two attackers involve language models by design: H1 is a language model acting as the focal provider, and H4 was written by a fresh session of an OpenAI model, started by the author, against the frozen defenders (Appendix~\ref{sec:app-design}). Drafts of the protocol, code and paper were reviewed by OpenAI GPT models and by Claude, read-only; each correction was checked against the repository before it was adopted. No AI tool is an author.
 
