197: 
198: \paragraph{How firm the reversals are.} The intervals in Table~\ref{tab:ph-churn} hold the six markets fixed. Treating the markets as a sample, Table~\ref{tab:ph-churn-t} gives exploratory $t$ intervals over the six market differences for every rate and search version: every one includes zero except B3 minus R3 at $p = \const{0.05}$ with the doubled searches. The churn reversals therefore have narrow seed-bootstrap intervals on these six markets, intervals that hold the selected policies fixed and omit search uncertainty, and they are not established beyond these markets. Market by market: at $p = \const{0.05}$ C$^*$ minus R3 is negative on \site{ch_d_5_neg} of the six markets and B3 minus R3 on \site{ch_q_5_neg} with the frozen searches, and on \site{ch_d_5_dneg} and \site{ch_q_5_dneg} with the doubled searches (C$^*$ minus R3: \site{ch_d_5_d}; B3 minus R3: \site{ch_q_5_d}); the frozen B3 value at this rate depends on one flagged cell. At $p = \const{0.03}$, C$^*$ minus R3 is negative on \site{ch_d_3_neg} of six markets with the frozen searches and on \site{ch_d_3_dneg} with the doubled ones, while B3 minus R3 is negative on \site{ch_q_3_neg} and \site{ch_q_3_dneg}, so its positive pooled value there does not hold market by market. At $p = \const{0.02}$, C$^*$ minus R3 is negative on only \site{ch_d_2_neg} markets: one market dominates the pooled value, and with the frozen searches it sets the sign. At $p = \const{0.01}$ the C$^*$ minus R3 difference is \site{ch_d_1_x} with the frozen searches and \site{ch_d_1_d} with the doubled ones, so the comparison with C$^*$ is not resolved at \const{0.01} or \const{0.02}, while the B3 minus R3 gap is \site{ch_q_1_x} and \site{ch_q_1_d}. \site{ch_inc} of the \site{ch_inc_n} doubling checks at $p = \const{0.01}$ and \const{0.05} and \site{ch_inc_mid} of the \site{ch_inc_mid_n} at \const{0.02} and \const{0.03} are flagged incomplete; the largest flagged change is \site{ch_flag_max}. Reselection within each rule's frozen reference menu under churn gives a nonzero training-set reference-score change in \site{ch_resel} of the \site{ch_resel_n} cells, with a largest absolute change of about \site{ch_resel_max}; this diagnostic does not bound the change in held-out gain, and the menus themselves were not regenerated.
